1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Ye static mock ya PPT nahi hai. Actual product Google Cloud Run par live hai,
and the operational badge comes from the real API.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:27,000
ProfileProof canonicalizes the LinkedIn URL, verifies identity,
normalizes professional fields, and attaches provenance.

3
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:43,000
The safe sample exercises the deployed API and full interface
without exposing anyone's private data.

4
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Raw JSON exposes source mode, warnings, limitations,
request ID, cache state, and the versioned schema.

5
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:15,000
This is a verified real-profile response from the stable GCP endpoint:
HTTP 200, public professional fields, provenance, and cached true.

6
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Invalid input fails before any upstream call. Redaction, rate limits,
session expiry, and response changes remain explicit.

7
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:46,000
LinkedIn blocks Google data-center egress, so Cloud Run uses an
automatically discovered residential worker on this Mac.

8
00:01:46,000 --> 00:02:01,000
If the Mac is off, GCP remains healthy but real acquisition reports
provider unavailable. An always-on home worker removes this limitation.

9
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:07,200
Typed data, verified identity, transparent provenance,
observability, caching, and honest failure behavior.
